IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — GOAL 1: GENERAL REQUIREMENTS.
--
--   "Does the applicant meet the residential requirement, and is any
--    general bar against receiving the benefit in the way?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_32.txt — ss 16, 18, 19.

§ `Goal 1 — general requirements`

-- Completed years of age on a date.
GIVEN dob IS A DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of someone born` dob `on` d MEANS
    IF   `add years` dob (DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR dob) AT MOST d
    THEN DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR dob
    ELSE DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR dob MINUS 1

-- s 16 "(2) A person (P) meets the residential requirement if— (a) P is a New
-- Zealand citizen or holds a residence class visa ..., and is ordinarily
-- resident in New Zealand when P first applies for the benefit, and— (i) has
-- resided continuously in New Zealand for a period of at least 2 years at any
-- one time after becoming a citizen or resident; or (ii) is recognised as a
-- refugee or a protected person ...; or (b) P is ordinarily resident in a
-- country with which New Zealand has a reciprocity agreement, and P has
-- resided continuously in New Zealand for a period of at least 2 years before
-- applying".
@ref s 16(2)
@export Whether a person meets the residential requirement for a main benefit under s 16 of the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ): a citizen or residence class visa holder, ordinarily resident in New Zealand when first applying, who has lived in New Zealand continuously for at least 2 years at a time since becoming a citizen or resident or is a recognised refugee or protected person; or someone ordinarily resident in a reciprocity country with 2 years' continuous residence in New Zealand before applying. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant  @desc Citizenship or visa, ordinary residence, continuous residence, refugee status and reciprocity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the residential requirement` a IF
        (    (   a's `immigration status` EQUALS `a New Zealand citizen`
              OR a's `immigration status` EQUALS `a residence class visa holder`)
         AND a's `ordinarily resident in New Zealand when first applying`
         AND (   a's `longest continuous residence since becoming a citizen or resident, in years` AT LEAST 2
              OR a's `a recognised refugee or protected person`))
    OR  (    a's `ordinarily resident in a reciprocity agreement country`
         AND a's `continuous residence in New Zealand before applying, in years` AT LEAST 2)

-- s 18 "A person is not entitled to receive at the same time, in his or her
-- own right,— (a) more than 1 main benefit ...; or (b) a main benefit ... and
-- New Zealand superannuation; or (c) a main benefit ... and a veteran's
-- pension." s 19 "(1) A person is not entitled or eligible to receive a
-- benefit if the person is— (a) unlawfully resident or present ...; or (b)
-- lawfully resident or present ... but only by virtue of holding a temporary
-- entry class visa."
@ref ss 18, 19(1)
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred by ss 18 or 19` a IF
        a's `receiving another main benefit, New Zealand superannuation or a veteran's pension`
    OR  a's `immigration status` EQUALS `unlawfully resident or present`
    OR  a's `immigration status` EQUALS `a temporary entry class visa holder`
